-- title:
--   An away-from-r unit of det-valuation one at level ℓ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and local data at $r$: a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible $\pi$, $\pi$-adic completeness, residue cardinality $\mathrm{Nat.card}(\mathcal O/(\pi))=r$ together with $(r)=(\pi)$, a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$, and a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$-algebra $Onr$ with an $\mathcal O$-automorphism $Fr$ such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$; finally a homomorphism $vdet:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by $vdet(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$. Let $\bar r$ be a prime with $\bar r\neq r$, let $N\neq 0$ be squarefree with $r\nmid N$ and $\bar r\nmid N$, and let $a_1,b_1<0$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ becomes a division algebra over the completion at a finite place exactly at the place containing $\bar r$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal order, $R_1\subseteq\Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ in one of them), $\iota_0$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$, and $v$ the height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$. Let $\Gamma^{t}$ be a subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ whose elements are exactly those of [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37), the intersection over all places $w\neq v$ of the preimages, under the localisation map at $w$, of the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$. Let $n_1$ be a finite-idelic unit in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` (lying in the adelic box of $R_1$, with $r\cdot n_1^{-1}$ in the box while $n_1^{-1}$ and $r^{-1}n_1$ are not) such that $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)=R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$. For each prime $\ell\neq r,\bar r$ let $s_\ell\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and $sf_\ell$ an idelic unit be given with: the component of $sf_\ell$ at every place not containing $r$ equal to $s_\ell\otimes 1$, its component at the place containing $r$ equal to $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of the central element $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lying in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; and let $\Gamma^{t}(\ell)=\Gamma^{t}\cap s_\ell\Gamma^{t}s_\ell^{-1}$. Then for each such $\ell$ there exists $w\in\Gamma^{t}$ with $w\in\Gamma^{t}(\ell)$ and $vdet(\iota_0(w))=1$.
--
--   This is the level-$\ell$ refinement of the statement that the away-from-$r$ unit group of an Eichler order contains an element of reduced norm $r$, i.e. an element of odd (indeed unit) determinant valuation in the $p$-adic uniformising group; the existence of such a $w$ is what makes the corresponding component of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation behave as required. It is used in the fine-moduli fibre computations for the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation tower.
